From: Onigiri
Subject: [PATCH] Report the folded camera state at every hinge angle

The inner panel never shows apps here, so the user always faces the cover and
the rear lenses. Stock firmware only reports the folded camera state (front
camera served by the rear sensor) while the hinge reads closed or tent; a
half-open or open reading switched video calls back to the covered inner lens.

diff --git a/smali_classes2/com/samsung/android/camera/CameraServiceWorker$DeviceStateListener.smali b/smali_classes2/com/samsung/android/camera/CameraServiceWorker$DeviceStateListener.smali
--- a/smali_classes2/com/samsung/android/camera/CameraServiceWorker$DeviceStateListener.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/com/samsung/android/camera/CameraServiceWorker$DeviceStateListener.smali
@@ -178,6 +178,8 @@
 
     :cond_4
     :goto_2
+    const-wide/16 v0, 0x6
+
     iget-object p0, p0, Lcom/samsung/android/camera/CameraServiceWorker$DeviceStateListener;->this$0:Lcom/samsung/android/camera/CameraServiceWorker;
 
     invoke-virtual {p0, v0, v1}, Lcom/samsung/android/camera/CameraServiceWorker;->notifyDeviceChange(J)V
